{"records":[{"id":"49g8777kmz","title":"The oncomicropeptide APPLE promotes hematopoietic malignancy by enhancing translation initiation. Sun et al","description":"Initiation is the rate-limiting step in translation, and its dysregulation is vital for carcinogenesis including hematopoietic malignancy. Thus, discovery of novel translation initiation regulators may provide promising therapeutic targets. Here, combining Ribo-seq, mass spectrometry and RNA-seq datasets, we discovered an oncomicropeptide, APPLE (a peptide located in ER), encoded by a noncoding RNA transcript in acute myeloid leukemia (AML). APPLE is overexpressed in various subtypes of AML and predicts a poor prognosis. The micropeptide is enriched in ribosomes and regulates the initiation step to enhance translation and to maintain high rates of oncoprotein synthesis. Mechanically, APPLE promotes PABPC1-eIF4G interaction, facilitates mRNA circularization and eIF4F initiation complex assembly to support a specific pro-cancer translation program. Targeting APPLE exhibited broad anti-cancer effects in vitro and in vivo. The study not only reports a previously unknown function of micropeptides, but also provides new opportunities for targeting the translation machinery in cancer cells.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-08-20T15:14:29.12Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/49g8777kmz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/49g8777kmz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yueqin","last_name":"Chen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"48xzrjhkp6","title":"Supplementary Material","description":"Supplementary Material of the manuscript titled\"Analysis of the noncoding RNA regulatory networks of H37Rv- and H37Rv△1759c-infected macrophages\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-05-16T15:46:29.752Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/48xzrjhkp6","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/48xzrjhkp6"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"wenqi","last_name":"dong","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Database"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"r99jg5d3bx","title":"Data for: Divergent Expressed Gene Identified and Interaction Prediction of Long Noncoding RNA and mRNA Involved In Duck Reproduction","description":"Supplementary table data for “Divergent Expressed Gene Identified and Interaction Prediction of Long Noncoding RNA and mRNA Involved In Duck Reproduction”.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2017-09-06T04:31:51.939Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/r99jg5d3bx","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/r99jg5d3bx"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jindong","last_name":"Ren","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Lizhi","last_name":"Lu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Junda","last_name":"Shen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Tao","last_name":"Zeng","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Hu","last_name":"Jian-Hong","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Li","last_name":"Chen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xue","last_name":"Du","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Clinical Support"],"journal_issn":["03784320"]},{"id":"sky4vt8xzh","title":"Western Blot","description":"Raw images of western blot in \"The noncoding circular RNA circHomer1 regulates synaptic development and experience-dependent plasticity in mouse visual cortex\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-07-28T14:35:59.01Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/sky4vt8xzh","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/sky4vt8xzh"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jacque","last_name":"Ip","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ying","last_name":"Cai","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"kds5f5hg8y","title":"Supplementary table for “Divergently Expressed Gene Identification and Interaction Prediction of Long Noncoding RNA and mRNA Involved In Duck Reproduction”","description":"Supplementary table for “Divergently Expressed Gene Identification and Interaction Prediction of Long Noncoding RNA and mRNA Involved In Duck Reproduction” which was submission to Animal Reproduction Science.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2017-04-24T02:50:12.326Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/kds5f5hg8y","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/kds5f5hg8y"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jindong","last_name":"Ren","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Supplementary Lighting"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"jtp6dcyp78","title":"GHG Mitigation beyond the NDC in Chile: An assessment of alternatives - Pyplan Models","description":"Models of Chilean GHG emissions of the transportation, industry and mining, buildings, IPPU, forestry, agriculture, waste and electricity generation sectors, used to explore mitigation opportunities beyond Chile's NDC . Data includes projection of emisions and mitigation actions.  We considered a baseline scenario where the Chilean NDC commitments are met. The mitigation actions considered in this scenario are what the team considered to be more plausible of occurring given the current policies in Chile, regardless of their cost.\nThe modelling was carried out based on the combination of scenarios and futures, where these two concepts are defined as follows:\n● \tFutures: They represent a trajectory of exogenous parameters that represent a possible set of conditions that could facilitate (or difficult) the mitigation strategies.\n●\tMitigation Scenarios: They represent different mitigation strategies implemented at a national level. Each scenario considers a set of mitigation actions and their specific level of implementation. \n We analyse two mitigation scenarios:\n●\tNDC Mitigation Scenario (NDC): Considers the achievement of all the mitigation commitments for 2030 done by Chile in its last NDC.\n●\tBeyond NDC Mitigation (NDC+): Considers enhanced mitigation actions to overachieve Chile's NDC commitments for 2030.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-06T07:41:49.603Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/jtp6dcyp78","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/jtp6dcyp78"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Rocío","last_name":"Herrera","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Diego","last_name":"Gonzalez","orcid":null},{"first_name":"José Miguel","last_name":"Valdés","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Lucas","last_name":"Maulén","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Climate Change Policy","Climate Change Model","Greenhouse Gas Abatement Cost","Greenhouse Gas Mitigation","Climate Data","Greenhouse Gas Policy"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"9pd453pm7k","title":"Long RNA-Sequencing Analysis of Extracellular Vesicles secreted by colorectal cancer cells","description":"Although much is known about extracellular miRNA, the identity, regulation, and functional roles of secreted coding and long noncoding RNAs (lncRNAs, &gt;200nt) are largely unknown. We have previously shown that mutant KRAS colorectal cancer (CRC) cells release EVs containing distinct proteomes, miRNAs, and circular RNAs. Here, we comprehensively identify the broad and diverse classes of CRC extracellular long RNAs secreted in EVs and demonstrate differential export of specific RNAs. We show that distinct noncoding RNAs including antisense transcripts and transcripts derived from pseudogenes are enriched in EVs compared to cellular profiles. Raw data from sequencing and analysis can be found at the supplied link (including the FASTQ data files). ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-09-04T16:46:14.504Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/9pd453pm7k","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/9pd453pm7k"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Scott","last_name":"Hinger","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Qi","last_name":"Liu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"James","last_name":"Patton","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["RNA Sequencing","Gene Ontology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"485swhn5tc","title":"Regulation of neuroregeneration by long noncoding RNAs","description":"Source data for panels in Ben-Tov Perry et al.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-09-07T09:03:11.804Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/485swhn5tc","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/485swhn5tc"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Igor","last_name":"Ulitsky","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Rotem","last_name":"Ben-Tov Perry","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Microscopy","Polymerase Chain Reaction","Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"cnwdsb8hdn","title":"Spatially Explicit database on crop-livestock management, soil, climate, greenhouse gas emissions and mitigation potential in Bangladesh","description":"This data article provides spatially explicit management information on crop-livestock production management together with greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions and mitigation potential at various jurisdiction level.  We collected crop and livestock management data and associated soil and climatic data from varieity of primary and secondary sources outlined below in methodology. The datafiles on crops and livestocks contain information on crop-livestock management, soil and climatic conditions and model output in terms of three greenhouse gases (CO2, CH4 and N2O) and global warming potential. The datafiles on mitigation potential contain district-level annual GHG mitigation potential by 2030 and 2050 segregated by different crops/livestock types and mitigation options. This unique dataset is useful for Bangladesh’s GHG accounting from agricultural sector and to update its nationally determined contributions. Jurisdiction-wise emissions and mitigation potential segregated by crop-livestock types and mitigation options is useful to prioritize agricultural research and development interventions at jurisdiction level consistent with their food production and GHG mitigation goal. \n\nThe crop data files i.e. “Crop_Baseline_2014-15.csv”, “Crop_BAU2030.csv”, “Crop_BAU2050.csv”, “Crop_MITI2030.csv” and “Crop_MITI2050.csv” contains plot-level information on crop management, soil and climatic conditions and model output in terms of three greenhouse gases (CO2, CH4 and N2O) and global warming potential. In these files, columns “A” to “BZ” contain plot-level information on specific crop management practices, soil and climatic conditions. Column “CA” onward in these file contain information about emission of individual GHGs and global warming potential (GWP). \n\nThe livestock data file i.e. “Livestock.csv” contains input and output data related to livestock. This data file contains information on livestock numbers at district level segregated by livestock type, breed, age, sex and management system. It also contains data on GHG arising from enteric fermentation and manure management, GHG mitigation potential of various mitigation options and total annual mitigation potential by 2030 and 2050. \n\nThe data files on mitigation potential by options i.e. “Mitigation_options&potential_2030.csv” and “Mitigation_options&potential_2050.csv” contain district-level annual GHG mitigation potential and associated abatement cost for different mitigation options, by 2030 and 2050, respectively. Similarly, data files on mitigation potential by crop/livestock type i.e. “Mitigation_potential_by_crop&livestock_type_2030.csv” and “Mitigation_potential_by_crop&livestock_type_2030.csv” contains district level annual GHG mitigation potential by each crop and livestock categories together with 95% margin of error. These files also contains crop, livestock and crop-livestock total annual mitigation potential by districts. \n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-06-10T20:26:12.323Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/cnwdsb8hdn","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/cnwdsb8hdn"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Tek B","last_name":"Sapkota","orcid":"0000-0001-5311-0586"},{"first_name":"Fahmida ","last_name":"Khanam","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Gokul Prasad ","last_name":"Mathivanan","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sylvia ","last_name":"Vetter","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sk. Ghulam","last_name":"Hussain","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Anne Laure","last_name":"Pilat","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sumona","last_name":"Shahrin","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Md. Khaled","last_name":"Hossain","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nathu Ram","last_name":"Sarker","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Timothy J","last_name":"Krupnik","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Applied Sciences","Natural Sciences"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"r6f44z6ycf","title":"Dataset of evaluation metrics for journalistic texts EN/SK","description":"The dataset contains automatic metrics calculated for English journalistic texts that where translated into Slovak language using four different machine translation systems (Google Translate Statistical Machine Translation, Google Translate Neural Machine Translation, MT@EC Statistical Machine Translation, E-Translation Neural Machine Translation). The automatic metrics are methods and techniques used for automated evaluation of the quality of machine translation. The dataset contains values for each machine translation system.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-09-30T06:46:11.711Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/r6f44z6ycf","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/r6f44z6ycf"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Lucia","last_name":"Benkova","orcid":"0000-0001-9629-1022"},{"first_name":"Dasa","last_name":"Munkova","orcid":"0000-0002-1003-7929"},{"first_name":"Lubomir","last_name":"Benko","orcid":"0000-0002-1657-395X"},{"first_name":"Michal","last_name":"Munk","orcid":"0000-0002-9913-3596"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Computer Science","Machine Translation"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":1285,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":20,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":1285,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":1277,"restricted":1,"embargoed":7},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/00djwmt25","name":"University Grants Committee","count":36},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":30},{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":20},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":11},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":8},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":6},{"id":"https://ror.org/01gavpb45","name":"Canadian Institutes of Health Research","count":5},{"id":"https://ror.org/05qx3fv49","name":"National Institute of Food and Agriculture","count":4},{"id":"https://ror.org/00k4n6c32","name":"European Commission","count":3},{"id":"https://ror.org/00snfqn58","name":"Fundação para a Ciência e Tecnologia","count":3}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":1273},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":5},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":3},{"id":"b121dfec-bb51-4f19-a2f6-bc9ce0197286","name":"Babeș-Bolyai University","count":1},{"id":"ea6ba14d-86b5-44fc-8476-80e67f7fc1af","name":"Demo Uni","count":1},{"id":"72c28c45-627f-446b-8a48-af7c0a51a357","name":"Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore","count":1},{"id":"f2ed6517-7fb4-4e02-8cef-95e75e9f0c9d","name":"Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University","count":1}],"top_institutions_stats":[{"id":"9d63ad1d-c391-5c35-a12e-cafe17017098","name":"Universidad Autonoma de Madrid","count":41},{"id":"33c40d0e-656e-5629-9810-2c8dbf2d0660","name":"Hong Kong Polytechnic University","count":21},{"id":"ecb64011-71f0-5223-b4e4-4d27d5f51d83","name":"Universidad Autonoma de Madrid Centro de Biologia Molecular Severo Ochoa","count":17},{"id":"e35a39f9-542c-422f-a692-5c6cafedd9b2","name":"Hong Kong Polytechnic University","count":16},{"id":"0ad97c43-5173-56e6-bbe6-46dad5323862","name":"Daffodil International University","count":14}]}}